James AI - Supabase update

Contents:
- server.js: updated server file

Before deploying:
1. Back up your current server.js and data/users.json.
2. Ensure package.json uses ES modules ("type": "module").
3. Install dependency in the project:
   npm install @supabase/supabase-js
4. In Render Environment, set:
   SUPABASE_URL = your Supabase project URL
   SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY = your Supabase secret key (server-side only)
5. Confirm the public.jamesai_user_data table exists with columns:
   google_sub TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
   email TEXT,
   user_data JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb,
   updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
6. Deploy and inspect Render logs. Test with a non-critical account before relying on it.

Never commit .env files or expose SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY in frontend code or chat.
Keep the original users.json backup until migration and plan/quota checks are complete.
